Agreements: Both use PLD with a KrF laser to grow YBCO films with Tsub as the key variable. Both use IBAD substrates and SrTiO3, and film thickness is about 200-250 nm. Both use oxygen pressure around 200-300 mTorr and post-anneal at 400 °C in flowing O2. The characterization matches: Δϕ from X-ray φ-scans, Tc from resistivity, and four-probe Jc at 65-77 K and 0-9 T with B//c. The analysis framework matches: GPR with transfer learning across chambers and a PAM using 1/Jc³ vs B.

Deviations: The groundtruth is a data-collection and modeling study with five sample series, different chambers and substrates, and RT versus TC Tsub measurement. Jc, Tc, Tsub and Δϕ are compiled into a database. GPR is trained on series 1 and transferred to series 2-5 with location-scale shift coefficients. Several PAM functions (1/Jc³, 1/Jc², log Jc, linear Jc) are compared, and the reference fields are 0 T at 77 K, 0.3 T at 65 K and 1 T at 65 K. The model output rewrites this as an optimization and validation plan with new elements:
- a baseline at unoptimized Tsub;
- an ablation study (omitting oxygenation, high versus low mosaic spread, CeO2 interface, cooling rates);
- Jc improvement >50% over baseline;
- ANOVA, R² ≥ 0.81 and triplicate samples;
- plume imaging;
- CORAL-based domain adaptation instead of LS shift;
- a 3 T extrapolation goal, and a Jc >3 MA/cm² target.

It also omits the five-series design, the RT/TC distinction, the specific reference fields, and the comparison of PAM functional forms. Its other numbers (Tsub 700-900 °C, 10-30 Hz versus 10 or 100 Hz, fluence) are only partly consistent.

The core technique and characterization overlap, but the sample design and experimental structure are substantially rewritten with new control and ablation groups. The score is therefore moderate.
